      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Flow Matching & Rectified Flows Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements 1-D flow matching on a two-mode Gaussian mixture. The vector field `v_\u03b8(x, t)` is a tiny MLP trained with the straight-line target. At inference, integrate 1, 2, 4, and 20 Euler steps and compare sample quality."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: training loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train_step(x0, net, rng, lr):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x1 = rng.gauss(0, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    t = rng.random()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x_t = t * x1 + (1 - t) * x0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    target = x1 - x0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pred = net_forward(x_t, t)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = (pred - target) ** 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # backprop + update"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: multi-step inference"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sample(net, num_steps):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = rng.gauss(0, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(num_steps):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t = 1.0 - i / num_steps"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        dt = 1.0 / num_steps"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x -= dt * net_forward(x, t)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: compare step counts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Expect the 4-step sampler to already match the 20-step quality \u2014 a big deal for latency."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `code/main.py` and compare 1-step vs 20-step MSE vs the true data distribution.\n2. **Medium.** Switch from uniform `t` sampling to logit-normal (concentrates sampling at mid-t). Does the model quality improve?\n3. **Hard.** Implement one reflow iteration: generate paired (x_0, x_1) by integrating the first model, train a second model on the pairs, and compare 1-step sample quality."
      ]
    }
